cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use SEMANTICA in research, please cite the software version you used. Method-specific references are documented in the methodological-foundations vignette."
title: "SEMANTICA: Semantic Item Generation and ACO-ESEM Scale Construction"
version: 0.2
authors:
  - family-names: "Cieza-Liza"
    given-names: "Pedro"
  - family-names: "Salas-Silva"
    given-names: "Reyniel"
  - family-names: "Gamarra-Moncayo"
    given-names: "José"
repository-code: "https://github.com/PedroCieza/SEMANTICA"
url: "https://PedroCieza.github.io/SEMANTICA/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - psychometrics
  - scale development
  - semantic embeddings
  - ant colony optimization
  - exploratory structural equation modeling
  - R package
abstract: >-
  SEMANTICA is an R package for semantic-assisted psychometric scale development
  and pre-data item screening. It combines LLM-assisted item generation, semantic
  embeddings, ant colony optimization, sample-free structural proxy diagnostics,
  optional participant-response validation, reproducibility tooling, and
  visualization.
